/candidate/codex-output.log:544:The target is the three-argument `any_int` predicate. I’m choosing an implementation that first performs explicit `isinstance(..., int)` checks, then tests the three possible sum equalities; this preserves the contract for floats instead of treating integral-valued floats as integers. The K semantics can therefore stay small but still model calls, boolean short-circuiting, integer addition, comparison, `if`, and `return` compositionally.
