The trusted retranslation is byte-identical to `solution.mpy`. Differential execution agrees on all 1,331 ordinary integer triples in `[-5,5]^3` and on the documented/branch-boundary cases, but it exposes concrete canonical divergences: `(True, 1, 2)`, `(False, 0, 0)`, and an `int` subclass `(1, 1, 2)` are `True` canonically and `False` in the generated program. I’m now rebuilding both LLVM concrete and Haskell proof definitions from copied source, then proving each of the seven claims separately.
